---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Pricing"
  description="Self-hosted Wicker Money is free and open source. A hosted version is a possibility being considered for the future, not a committed product with a price."
>
  <section class="wmm-section wmm-page-hero">
    <div class="wmm-container">
      <p class="wmm-eyebrow">Pricing</p>
      <h1>Self-hosted is free. That's not an intro offer.</h1>
      <p class="wmm-lede">
        There's no free tier designed to convert you into a paid one. Self-hosting is
        the product, and it costs whatever it costs you to run a small Docker container
        next to a Postgres database you already have or can add cheaply.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wmm-section wmm-section--alt">
    <div class="wmm-container wmm-pricing-grid">
      <div class="wmm-card wmm-pricing-card">
        <h2>Self-hosted</h2>
        <p class="wmm-price">$0</p>
        <p>Run it yourself on your own hardware or a small VPS.</p>
        <ul class="wmm-checklist">
          <li>Full application, AGPL-3.0</li>
          <li>All bundled plugins</li>
          <li>Your data never leaves your infrastructure</li>
          <li>No account limits, no feature gates</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="wmm-btn-row">
          <a class="wmm-btn wmm-btn--primary" href="/self-hosting">Get started</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="wmm-card wmm-pricing-card wmm-pricing-card--future">
        <h2>Hosted</h2>
        <p class="wmm-price">Not available</p>
        <p>
          A hosted version is something we're considering, not something we've built or
          priced. If self-hosting isn't for you, it isn't ready yet &mdash; there's no
          waitlist to join today.
        </p>
        <div class="wmm-btn-row">
          <a class="wmm-btn wmm-btn--secondary" href="https://github.com/wickermoney/wicker-money">Follow progress on GitHub</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wmm-section">
    <div class="wmm-container">
      <h2>What "free" actually means here</h2>
      <p class="wmm-lede" style="max-width: 72ch;">
        No investors, no advertising business model, no data broker deal funding the
        gap. The application and bundled plugins are licensed AGPL-3.0; the plugin SDK
        and UI kit &mdash; the surface a plugin builds against &mdash; are Apache-2.0. Nothing
        here is a loss-leader for a subscription upsell.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .wmm-pricing-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
      gap: var(--wm-gap);
    }
    .wmm-pricing-card h2 {
      margin: 0 0 4px;
    }
    .wmm-pricing-card--future {
      opacity: 0.85;
    }
    .wmm-price {
      font-size: 2rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      margin: 0 0 12px;
    }
    .wmm-checklist {
      list-style: none;
      padding: 0;
      margin: 16px 0 0;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 8px;
      color: var(--wm-text-muted);
    }
    .wmm-checklist li {
      padding-left: 24px;
      position: relative;
    }
    .wmm-checklist li::before {
      content: '\2713';
      position: absolute;
      left: 0;
      color: var(--wm-positive);
      font-weight: 700;
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
